From a5bfcf0109f270cb482ec4e3588b22424dd3aa2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Fritz <gh@chaos4all.de>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:37:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] ipa: libipa: camera_sensor_helper: Add OV8858 black level

The ov8858 kernel driver programs the sensor's BLC target register
(0x4005) to 0x10 in all modes, so the black level is 16 at 10 bits. A
measurement with the lens covered on an HP Pro x2 612 G2 gives 14.75 to
16 per channel.

Report it from the sensor helper so that IPAs which get the black level
from the helper use the right value. This changes the black level used
by the Mali-C55 and simple IPAs, and by the rkisp1 IPA when its tuning
file enables black level correction without levels, for the OV8858.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Richard Fritz <gh@chaos4all.de>
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
index 9457d62b3..fad57daec 100644
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -803,6 +803,9 @@ public:
 		 * See: https://patchwork.linuxtv.org/project/linux-media/patch/20221106171129.166892-2-nicholas@rothemail.net/#142267
 		 */
 		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 128 };
+
+		/* From Linux kernel driver: BLC target 0x10 at 10 bits. */
+		blackLevel_ = 1024;
 	}
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov8858", CameraSensorHelperOv8858)
